.\" sliver-config(5). Spec: docs/customization.md (elm). A test checks that every module type,
.\" common module key, context key and bar gesture known to crates/sliver-config is listed here.
.TH SLIVER\-CONFIG 5 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sliver\-config \- Touch Bar configuration (config.toml)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliver/config.toml
.br
.I /etc/xdg/sliver/config.toml
.br
.I /usr/share/sliver/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Touch Bar is configured the way waybar is: everything on it is a
.IR module ,
every module is shaped by configuration
.RB ( format ,
states, gesture bindings), the look comes from a stylesheet
.RB ( sliver\-stylesheet (5)),
and zones, layers, layouts and rules are all defined by the user.
The file is TOML.
Keys are kebab\-case and use waybar's names wherever the concept maps, so waybar module blocks port with few changes
(or use
.BR "sliverctl config import\-waybar" ).
.PP
The first file that exists in the order above is used.
The built\-in defaults are always merged underneath it, so the
.BR base ,
.B fn
and
.B media
layers, the
.BR default ,
.B fkeys
and
.B media
layouts and the control strip exist even with an empty file.
Any of them can be redefined.
.PP
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
watches the file, its includes and the stylesheet, and applies changes when they are saved.
An invalid configuration is never applied: the last good one stays live and the errors are reported.
Unknown keys produce warnings, not errors.
Check a file with
.BR "sliverctl config check" .
.SH TOP\-LEVEL KEYS
.TP
.BR version " = 1"
Format version.
.TP
.BR include " = [" \fIpaths\fP ]
Other files to merge in.
Paths are relative to the including file, and
.B ~
and globs work.
Tables are merged deeply, the including file wins, and earlier includes win over later ones.
Arrays are replaced, not concatenated.
.TP
.BR stylesheet " = " \fIpath\fP
Default:
.B style.css
next to the configuration.
.B style\-dark.css
and
.B style\-light.css
follow the desktop's color scheme when present.
.TP
.BR theme " = " sliver | light | high\-contrast | classic
The built\-in theme under the stylesheet (default
.BR sliver ).
See
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5).
.SH [bar]
.TP
.B name
Becomes a CSS class on the bar.
.TP
.BR spacing ", " margin
Pixels between modules, and around the strip.
.TP
.BR fn\-mode " = " hold | toggle
What the Fn key does with the
.B fn
layer.
.TP
.BR fire\-on " = " press | release
When taps fire, by default.
Each module can override it.
.SH [display]
.TP
.BR brightness " = " adaptive | fixed
Adaptive follows the main screen.
.TP
.BR max\-brightness " = " 0\-255
.TP
.BR dim\-after ", " off\-after
Durations (default 30s and 60s), or
.BR """never""" .
.TP
.BR pixel\-shift " = " true | false
.TP
.B [display.on\-battery]
.BR max\-brightness ,
.B dim\-after
and
.B off\-after
to use instead while running on battery (from UPower).
Keys left out keep their
.B [display]
values.
For example, a dimmer bar that turns off sooner:
.B max\-brightness = 60
and
.BR "off\-after = ""20s""" .
.SH [apps], [providers] AND [api]
What apps and scripts that use the D\-Bus API may put on the bar.
Your own layouts and rules always win over them.
.TP
.BR [apps."\fIapp\-id\fP"]
.B controls
(default true): the app's items may fill
.BR app\-controls .
.B whole\-bar
(default true): it may take over the whole bar.
.B pin
= \fIprovider\fP: only that provider fills the app's controls.
App ids match case\-insensitively, with a
.B .desktop
suffix ignored.
.B [apps."*"]
sets the defaults for every app.
.TP
.BR [providers."\fIid\fP"]
.B show
(default true): show this provider's items.
.B allow
(default false): let a sandboxed (Flatpak or Snap) provider show status items.
.B order
= \fIn\fP: its place among status items.
.TP
.B [api]
.B target
(default true): let clients put controls on the bar for another app.
.PP
The agent applies changes to these tables on reload, without restarting clients.
.SH LAYERS, LAYOUTS AND RULES
.TP
.B [layers]
Maps each layer name to its default layout.
.B base
and
.B fn
are reserved (Fn shows
.BR fn ).
Any other name is a custom layer, opened by a
.B layer
action.
.TP
.BI [layer\-options. name ]
.B timeout
(a duration) and
.B close\-button
(a boolean).
.TP
.BI [layouts. name ]
.B extends
names a parent layout.
.B zones
is an ordered array of tables with
.BR name ,
.B modules
(module ids or inline tables),
.B width
.RB ( """auto""" ,
pixels or
.BR """fill""" ),
.B align
.RB ( start ,
.BR center ,
.BR end ),
.B module\-width
(the default width for the zone's modules) and
.BR class .
A child layout's zone replaces the parent's zone of the same name, in place.
.B zone\-order
sets the order of zones the child adds.
Zones become stylesheet classes
.RB ( .zone\- \fIname\fP ).
.TP
.B [[rules]]
.BR name ,
.B when
(a condition),
.B layer
(default
.BR base )
and
.BR layout .
Rules are checked top to bottom, and the first match wins.
If none matches, the
.B [layers]
default applies.
.SH CONDITIONS
A condition
.RB ( when ,
on rules and on modules) is a table of context keys, all of which must match.
.B any = [{...}, {...}]
needs one of the sub\-tables to match, and
.B not = {...}
negates.
A value can be a literal, an array (one of),
.BR "{ regex = ""..."" }" ,
.BR "{ contains = ""..."" }" ,
.BR "{ below = N }" ,
.B "{ above = N }"
or
.BR "{ between = [A, B] }" .
Keys are case\-insensitive, and
.B \-
and
.B _
are interchangeable.
An unknown or unavailable key never matches.
.PP
Context keys:
.TP
Focus
.BR app_id ,
.BR desktop_id ,
.BR title ,
.BR pid ,
.BR fullscreen ,
.BR floating ,
.BR xwayland
.TP
Desktop
.BR workspace ,
.BR workspace_name ,
.BR special_workspace ,
.BR monitor ,
.BR monitors ,
.BR external_display ,
.BR keyboard_layout ,
.BR submap ,
.B screencast
.TP
Session
.BR locked ,
.BR idle ,
.BR sleeping ,
.BR dnd ,
.BR dark_mode ,
.B caffeine
.TP
Power
.BR on_battery ,
.BR battery_pct ,
.BR battery_state ,
.BR lid_closed ,
.B power_profile
.TP
Media and audio
.BR media_status ,
.BR media_player ,
.BR media_title ,
.BR media_artist ,
.BR mic_muted ,
.BR output_muted ,
.B volume
.TP
Other
.BR brightness ,
.BR time ,
.BR weekday ,
.BR physical_esc ,
.BR layer ,
.BR layout ,
.B app_controls
(true while an app fills App controls, so a layout can show something else when none does)
.PP
User variables set with
.B sliverctl var set
can be used too.
.SH MODULES
A module reference is
.IR type ,
.IR type # instance
or
.IR namespace / name [# instance ],
and is configured in
.BI [modules." reference "]\fR.
The instance becomes a CSS class.
.B key/\fIName\fP
(for example
.BR key/F1 ,
.BR key/PlayPause )
needs no block.
A zone's
.B modules
list can also contain inline tables with a
.B type
key.
Built\-in modules have no powers that user modules lack.
.SS Module types
.BR key ,
.BR spacer ,
.BR clock ,
.BR battery ,
.BR backlight ,
.BR backlight/slider ,
.BR kbd\-backlight ,
.BR kbd\-backlight/slider ,
.BR audio ,
.BR audio/slider ,
.BR mpris ,
.BR workspaces ,
.BR window ,
.BR mode ,
.BR language ,
.BR idle\-inhibitor ,
.BR dnd ,
.BR dark\-mode ,
.BR power\-profiles ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR memory ,
.BR temperature ,
.BR disk ,
.BR load ,
.BR network ,
.BR bluetooth ,
.B graph
.RB ( custom\-graph/ \fIname\fP ),
.BR privacy ,
.BR systemd\-failed\-units ,
.BR taskbar ,
.BR notifications ,
.BR emoji ,
.BR timer ,
.BR image ,
.B group
.RB ( group/ \fIname\fP ),
.B app\-controls
and
.B status\-items
(where items published by apps go;
.B tray
is an alias),
.B app
.RB ( app/ \fIprovider\fP # \fIitem\fP
pins one published item), and
.B custom
.RB ( custom/ \fIname\fP ).
waybar's names
.RB ( pulseaudio ,
.BR hyprland/workspaces ,
.BR idle_inhibitor ,
\&...) are accepted as aliases.
.SS Common keys
Every module accepts these.
waybar's names are accepted as aliases:
.BR on\-click ,
.BR on\-double\-click ,
.BR on\-click\-right ,
.BR on\-click\-release ,
.BR on\-scroll\-up ,
.BR on\-scroll\-down ,
.BR tooltip ,
.BR tooltip\-format ,
.BR smooth\-scrolling\-threshold .
.TP
.B format
Text with
.BI { placeholder }
and
.BI { name : spec }
(strftime for the clock).
A subset of Pango markup is allowed.
.TP
.BR format\-alt ", " format\- \fIstate\fP ", " format\- \fIstatus\fP ", " format\- \fIstatus\fP \- \fIstate\fP
Alternatives, chosen in that order (most specific first).
A tap toggles
.B format\-alt
when
.B on\-tap
is unset.
.TP
.B format\-icons
An array (indexed by percentage), a table (by alt, status, state, then
.BR default ),
or a string.
An entry can be
.B { icon = "name\-or\-path" }
for an image.
.TP
.B states
Name to threshold, for example
.BR "{ warning = 30, critical = 15 }" .
Adds a class and selects
.BR format\- \fIstate\fP .
.TP
.BR icon ", " icon\-theme ", " icon\-size
XDG icon name, file path, or
.BI tiny\-dfr: name\fR.
.TP
.B width
.BR """auto""" ,
pixels,
.B """fill"""
or
.BR "{ fill = N }" .
.B expand = true
means
.BR """fill""" .
.TP
.BR min\-length ", " max\-length ", " align ", " justify
Label length in characters (ellipsized), and alignment.
.TP
.B class
Extra CSS classes.
.TP
.B when
A condition.
The module is shown only while it holds.
.TP
.B hide\-empty\-text
Hide the module when its text is empty.
.TP
.BR detail ", " detail\-format
There is no hover on a touch strip.
The detail is the accessible description and the hold\-to\-peek overlay.
.TP
.BR fire\-on ", " repeat ", " swipe\-threshold
Tap on press or release, hold\-to\-repeat, and swipe distance in pixels.
.TP
.BR on\-tap ", " on\-double\-tap ", " on\-hold ", " on\-release ", " on\-swipe\-left ", " on\-swipe\-right ", " on\-drag ", " on\-update
Actions (see ACTIONS).
Binding
.B on\-double\-tap
delays single taps on that module.
.TP
.B actions
Gesture to built\-in module action, for example
.BR "{ on\-hold = ""mode"" }" .
.TP
.BR menu ", " menu\-trigger
An array of
.B {label, icon, on\-tap}
shown as a temporary sub\-bar with a close button, and the gesture that opens it.
.TP
.B interval
Polling period
.RB ( """5s""" )
or
.BR """once""" .
The floor is 100\ ms.
.TP
.B pass\-through
For
.B app/
modules: also send the gesture to the app when a user
.B on\-*
binding exists.
By default the user's binding replaces the app's event.
.SS Groups
.BI group/ name
takes
.BR modules ,
.B orientation
.RB ( horizontal
or
.BR vertical )
and
.BR drawer ,
a table with
.B reveal
.RB ( tap ,
.BR hold ,
.BR swipe ),
.B mode
.RB ( inline
or
.BR bar ),
.BR start\-expanded ,
.BR collapse\-after ,
.BR transition\-duration ,
.B children\-class
and
.BR transition\-left\-to\-right .
.SS Custom modules
.BI custom/ name
runs scripts the way waybar does.
.TP
.BR exec ", " exec\-if
The command (run with
.BR "sh \-c" ,
never as root) and its guard.
.TP
.BR interval ", " signal
Run on a timer, on
.B SIGRTMIN+\fIn\fP
or
.BR "sliverctl signal" .
With neither, the script runs continuously and each output line is an update.
.TP
.B restart\-interval
For continuous scripts that exit (minimum 1 s, with backoff).
.TP
.B exec\-on\-event
Re\-run after an
.B on\-*
action (default true).
.TP
.B return\-type
.B """"""
(lines: text, detail, class) or
.B """json"""
(one object per line with
.BR text ,
.BR alt ,
.BR tooltip ,
.BR class ,
.BR percentage ,
.BR icon ,
.BR value ,
.BR hidden ).
.TP
.BR escape ", " timeout ", " env
Escape markup, per\-run timeout (default 2 s), and extra environment.
Commands also get
.BR SLIVER_MODULE ,
.BR SLIVER_LAYER ,
.B SLIVER_LAYOUT
and
.BR SLIVER_APP_ID .
.SH ACTIONS
An
.B on\-*
key takes one of:
.TP
.I """command"""
A shell command.
.B {value}
is substituted for
.BR on\-drag .
.TP
.B { exec = [argv] }
No shell.
.TP
.BR "{ key = ""F5"" }" ", " "{ keys = [""LeftCtrl"", ""LeftAlt"", ""F1""] }"
Key presses (combos are released in reverse).
Key names are tiny\-dfr's
.RB ( F1 ,
.BR BrightnessDown ,
.BR PlayPause ,
\&...).
.TP
.BR "{ layer = ""media"", mode = ""toggle"" }" ", " "{ close\-layer = true }"
.B mode
is
.BR hold ,
.B toggle
or
.BR oneshot .
.TP
.BR "{ layout = N }" ", " "{ open = ""app.desktop"" }" ", " "{ url = U }"
.TP
.B { dbus = { bus, dest, path, interface, method, args } }
.TP
.BR "{ signal = N }" ", " "{ update = ""custom/vpn"" }" ", " "{ format = ""toggle\-alt"" }" ", " "{ module\-action = NAME }"
.TP
.I [ step, ... ]
A macro.
Steps can include
.BR "{ sleep = ""100ms"" }" .
Macros are capped at 32 steps and 10 s.
.PP
Bar\-wide gestures go in
.BR [gestures] :
.BR two\-finger\-swipe\-left ,
.BR two\-finger\-swipe\-right ,
.BR edge\-swipe\-from\-left ,
.BR edge\-swipe\-from\-right .
.PP
Durations are written
.BR """250ms""" ,
.BR """5s""" ,
.B """2m"""
or as a bare number of seconds.
.SH WHAT CANNOT BE CONFIGURED
Every layout, including the Fn layer, is fully editable and may drop Escape and the F\-keys.
Pressing Fn twice and holding it always shows the built\-in F1\(enF12 layer (with Esc on bars that have no physical Escape key).
This is enforced by
.BR sliverd (8),
and no configuration can change it.
.PP
App items, custom module output and notification text are never shown on the lock screen.
Intervals have a 100\ ms floor, and scripts have timeouts.
A configuration error never reaches the bar.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
version = 1

[layers]
base = "default"
fn = "fkeys"

[[layouts.default.zones]]
name = "main"
width = "fill"
modules = ["app\-controls"]

[[layouts.default.zones]]
name = "controls"
modules = ["status\-items", "battery", "clock"]

[[rules]]
name = "Terminals get F\-keys"
when = { app\-id = ["foot", "kitty"] }
layout = "fkeys"

[modules.battery]
states = { warning = 30, critical = 15 }
format = "{icon} {capacity}%"
format\-icons = ["empty", "low", "half", "high", "full"]

[modules."custom/vpn"]
exec = "~/bin/vpn\-status \-\-json"
return\-type = "json"
interval = "5s"
signal = 8
on\-tap = "~/bin/vpn\-toggle"
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5),
.BR sliverctl (1),
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliverd (8),
.BR waybar (5)
.PP
.I docs/customization.md
in the sliver sources (the full specification).
